rota lap 4427, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; advanced past the previous Fire row's repeat. The threshold and three readings called for testing the recovered tools and running recovery twice before trusting it.
obs Restored five original log files, six cited archive pages, and the link-touch and plant-liveness scan, control, and witness files from stash f5d163e930fb2d0a721a6dc6558daa641669bae2. The second restoration changed no bytes. All original recovered files matched that stash.
obs The mutation scan checks sed's exit status before comparing complete output. It separates the input from redirects, disables sed command and file operations, and bounds each program by time and output size. Its capability probe is shared with the roster runner. Unresolved inputs remain outside this partial shell reader's proof.
obs The link-touch control proves the current commit hook in real repositories. The shared hook remains unchanged. Diffuser's published watcher comments and executable modes remain whole; Bakery's competing parked watcher draft was not replayed.
obs Restored the original shelf rows and derived both closed-day rosters from their actual rows. The five logs name 43 file paths, all present after recovery. Three recovered REDS drafts keep their original local numbers inside quotations; they add no published ledger rows.
obs The cold pass finished with tree_moved=no. stash_record named five unlanded logs. The closing roster scan also named plant_liveness as an unrostered older run record. Restoring the logs and its roster entry addresses both findings.
obs The previous lap's hot process still ran after round-open parked its staged tree. Its transcript named 18 stashes against 19 here, so it could not verify this lap. Saved that transcript and sent TERM only to its verified local PID 1040642 through fleet_call. No peer process was signaled.
obs Two detached launches left only a header. Keeping the calling command shell alive allowed the next detached pass to run to completion. The fresh transcript named this HEAD and all 19 stashes; its exact tool-returned path was used.
obs Both remotes were pulled before restoration. The seed publish, scrub design, naming rulings, and other handoff custody gates remain held.
